---
/**
 * Consultancy Services (/services) — the ★ reusable template page (docs/consultancy-build-plan.md).
 * Built against the committed Figma node 8119:7174
 * (design/figma/fTqnnV20l9htP7vFJrOsvn/8119-7174/). Content lives in `@lib/services-content`,
 * kept separate from this file so future sub-page riffs can reuse the same shape.
 *
 * The page is now assembled entirely from shared components — `SubPageHero`, five
 * `ServiceDetailSection`s and `CtaSection` — after the test-registration sub-pages confirmed
 * each of those is genuinely the same Figma unit rather than a per-page treatment. See each
 * component's header for the geometry and typography audit it owns.
 *
 * Typography confirmed against node.json (not guessed):
 *   - Hero "Study Abroad": 64/56/700/−0.26. First recorded here as "a one-off combination…
 *     for a single page's title" — that was wrong. All seven sub-page heroes use it, so it is
 *     now the named `--type-page-title` role (see tokens.css) applied via `SubPageHero`.
 *   - Section titles, sub-headings and body copy: owned by `ServiceDetailSection`.
 *   - Spacing/radii: every gap/padding on this page (80px between section title and body, 40px
 *     column gap, 24px within a block, 120px page rhythm) already exists in the snapped scale
 *     from Home's build — no new spacing tokens needed.
 *
 * Content notes (confirmed via node.json, not guessed):
 *   - "Admission Processing" and "Tuition & Acceptance Fee Payments" duplicate another
 *     section's about/covers copy word-for-word in the source — the design's real
 *     not-yet-personalised state (`@lib/services-content` header comment), kept as-is, same
 *     precedent as Home's repeated team/testimonial placeholders.
 *   - Only the HEALS-content "about" paragraphs carry a bold-italic accent-warm lead sentence
 *     ("Studying abroad shouldn't come down to who you know.") — confirmed via
 *     `characterStyleOverrides`; the Scholarship/Career/Tuition about paragraphs have none.
 *   - The closing CTA band is the shared `CtaSection.astro`. This page's node.json agrees with
 *     Home's, About's and Team's byte-for-byte, so it is instantiated rather than re-authored;
 *     see that file for the confirmed content and geometry. (An earlier note here recorded the
 *     arrowless buttons as a difference *from* Home. That was wrong: Home's own CTA button
 *     instances also carry `ArrowRight` at `visible: false` — Home was simply rendering arrows
 *     the design never had, which is the drift this shared component removed.)
 *   - Every cost row's second grid column is an empty container in the source (spacing/balance
 *     only). Each section carries three blocks, so the grid's fourth cell is simply never
 *     filled — the same result, without a dummy element.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SubPageHero from '@components/SubPageHero.astro';
import ServiceDetailSection from '@components/ServiceDetailSection.astro';
import CtaSection from '@components/CtaSection.astro';
import { heroTitle, services } from '@lib/services-content';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Services — GIEVA Consultancy"
  description="From test registration to study-abroad advising — explore every GIEVA consultancy service, what it covers, and what it costs."
  brand="consultancy"
>
  <SubPageHero title={heroTitle} />

  <!-- ── Service details + CTA ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section services-body">
    <div class="container services-body__list">
      {services.map((service) => <ServiceDetailSection {...service} />)}

      <CtaSection />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Hero ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* The hero's styles live in src/components/SubPageHero.astro, which owns the markup for
     every Consultancy sub-page hero. */

  /* ── Service details + CTA ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .services-body {
    padding-block: var(--space-6xl);
  }
  .services-body__list {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6xl);
  }

  /* ── CTA (same content/shape as Home's) ────────────────────────────────── */
  /* The CTA band's styles live in src/components/CtaSection.astro, which owns the
     markup for all four Consultancy pages. */
</style>
